  "summary": "Records from UNC Charlotte show the Houston Police Department searched the university's Flock ALPR network over 183,000 times from March\u2013May 2026, far more than local agencies. The story raises concerns about nationwide data sharing and weak cross-state guardrails, noting Appalachian State and UNC Chapel Hill have turned off national sharing while HPD says it is investigating its usage.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The law enforcement agency conducted searches that included the UNC Charlotte network more than 183,000 times from March through May 2026.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "Under North Carolina law, you can't sell the data. Texas has no guardrails.",
      "paragraph_idx": 17
    },
    {
      "quote": "The use of automated license plate recognition systems by Houston Police Department personnel is regularly reviewed. The department has identified usage that is being investigated further.",
      "paragraph_idx": 14
    },
    {
      "quote": "Appalachian State University turned off national sharing of its Flock network, and UNC Chapel Hill made the same decision last week.",
      "paragraph_idx": 21
    }
  ],
